# =============================================================================
# MLOps Energy Forecast — Secrets Template
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to secrets/.env and fill in your values.
# secrets/.env is gitignored — never commit real credentials.
#
# Also create secrets/postgres_password.txt with the database password.
# For ENTSO-E downloads inside Docker, create secrets/entsoe_api_token.txt
# with the API key (mounted as ENTSOE_API_TOKEN_FILE for the api service).
# For local runs, set ENTSOE_API_KEY instead — configure exactly one source.
#
# Usage: docker compose --env-file secrets/.env up
# =============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENTSO-E API key — exactly ONE source per runtime (see _read_api_key in
# src/ingestion/entsoe.py). Setting both at once is a configuration error.
#
# | Runtime              | Source                                             |
# |----------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
# | Local pytest / CLI   | ENTSOE_API_KEY env var (export, never committed)   |
# | Docker `api` service | secrets/entsoe_api_token.txt -> ENTSOE_API_TOKEN_FILE |
#
# Local example (PowerShell):
#   $env:ENTSOE_API_KEY = (Get-Content secrets/entsoe_api_token.txt -Raw).Trim()
#   python -m src ingest
# Local example (Bash):
#   export ENTSOE_API_KEY="$(cat secrets/entsoe_api_token.txt)"
#   python -m src ingest
# Without a key, `make ingest`/`python -m src ingest` aborts with a
# RuntimeError unless data.entsoe.allow_synthetic: true is set explicitly
# (offline dev/CI only — never production training).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# PostgreSQL (non-sensitive config — password goes in secrets/postgres_password.txt)
POSTGRES_DB=mlflow
POSTGRES_USER=mlflow